These define how well the application should work.

NFR-1 Performance
Dashboard loads quickly.
AI summaries appear with a loading indicator.
File uploads provide progress feedback.
NFR-2 Security
Passwords are hashed.
JWT authentication.
Input validation.
File type validation.
File size limits.
Protection against common web vulnerabilities such as XSS and injection attacks.
NFR-3 Accessibility

The application should be usable by as many people as possible.

Examples:

Keyboard navigation
Good color contrast
Screen reader support
Descriptive alt text
Proper labels for form inputs
NFR-4 Responsive Design

Support:

Mobile
Tablet
Laptop
Desktop
NFR-5 Scalability

Architecture should allow future additions without major rewrites.

Example future features:

Voice explanations
AI chatbot
Wearable integrations
NFR-6 Reliability

If OCR or AI fails:

Show a clear error message.
Allow the user to retry.
Preserve the uploaded report where appropriate.
NFR-7 Maintainability

Code should be:

Modular
Reusable
Well documented
Consistently formatted
Easy to test
NFR-8 Privacy

Medical reports contain sensitive information.

Therefore:

Use HTTPS in production.
Restrict access so users can only view their own reports.
Avoid storing unnecessary personal data.
Keep AI prompts limited to the information needed for generating explanations.
